["function","Check if collection exists in database\n\nChecks if the Collection object refers to a collection in the database (schema).",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if collection exists in the database, else <type>false<\/type> if it does not.\n\nA table defined with two columns (doc and _id) is considered a collection,  and a third _json_schema column as of MySQL 8.0.21.  Adding an additional column means existsInDatabase() will no longer see it as a collection."]]
["function","Search for document\n\nSearch a database collection for a document or set of documents. The found documents are returned as a CollectionFind object is to further modify or fetch results from.",[["$search_condition","string","Although optional, normally a condition is defined to limit the results to a subset of documents.\n\nMultiple elements might build the condition and the syntax supports parameter binding.  The expression used as search condition must be a valid SQL expression. If no search condition is provided (field empty) then find('true') is assumed."]],["mysql_xdevapi\\CollectionFind","A CollectionFind object to verify the operation, or fetch the found documents."]]
