["function","Execute operation with EXCLUSIVE LOCK\n\nLocks the document exclusively. As long as the document is locked, other transactions can't update the document, use SELECT ... LOCK IN SHARE MODE, or read the data in certain transaction isolation levels. Consistent reads ignore any locks set on the records that exist in the read view.\n\nTo avoid concurrency problems, it makes sense to use this function with the mysql_xdevapi\\Collection::modify method. Essentially, this function uses row locks to serialise access to rows.",[["$lock_waiting_option","int","Optional waiting option. By default it is <constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_DEFAULT<\/constant>. Valid values are these constants:\n\n<constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_DEFAULT<\/constant>\n\n<constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_NOWAIT<\/constant>\n\n<constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_SKIP_LOCKED<\/constant>"]],["mysql_xdevapi\\CollectionFind","Returns a CollectionFind object that can be used for further processing."]]
["function","Execute operation with SHARED LOCK\n\nAllows to share the documents between multiple transactions which are locking in shared mode.\n\nOther sessions can read the rows, but cannot modify them until your transaction commits.\n\nIf any of these rows were changed by another transaction that hasn't been committed, the query will wait until that transaction has ended to be able to use the latest values.",[["$lock_waiting_option","int","Optional waiting option. By default it is <constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_DEFAULT<\/constant>. Valid values are these constants:\n\n<constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_DEFAULT<\/constant>\n\n<constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_NOWAIT<\/constant>\n\n<constant>MYSQLX_LOCK_SKIP_LOCKED<\/constant>"]],["mysql_xdevapi\\CollectionFind","A CollectionFind object that can be used for further processing"]]
