["function","Returns new DateTime object\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::__construct but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>. Consider using the <classname>DateTimeImmutable<\/classname> and features instead.\n\nReturns a new DateTime object.",[["$datetime","string","A date\/time string. Valid formats are explained in Date and Time Formats.\n\nEnter <literal>\"now\"<\/literal> here to obtain the current time when using the <parameter>$timezone<\/parameter> parameter."],["$timezone","DateTimeZone|null","A <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object representing the timezone of <parameter>$datetime<\/parameter>.\n\nIf <parameter>$timezone<\/parameter> is omitted or <type>null<\/type>, the current timezone will be used.\n\nThe <parameter>$timezone<\/parameter> parameter and the current timezone are ignored when the <parameter>$datetime<\/parameter> parameter either is a UNIX timestamp (e.g. <literal>@946684800<\/literal>) or specifies a timezone (e.g. <literal>2010-01-28T15:00:00+02:00<\/literal>)."]],["mixed","Returns a new DateTime instance."],["DateTimeImmutable::__construct"]]
