["function","Clear a field or all fields\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nClears either all of the fields or a specific field. A cleared field is marked as unset, giving it the lowest priority against overlapping fields or even default values when calculating the time. Additionally, its value is set to <literal>0<\/literal>, though given the fieldÊ¼s low priority, its value may have been internally set to another value by the time the field has finished been queried.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$field","int|null","One of the <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> date\/time field constants. These are integer values between <literal>0<\/literal> and <constant>IntlCalendar::FIELD_COUNT<\/constant>."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Create a new IntlCalendar\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGiven a timezone and locale, this method creates an <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> object. This factory method may return a subclass of <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname>.\n\nThe calendar created will represent the time instance at which it was created, based on the system time. The fields can all be cleared by calling <function>IntCalendar::clear<\/function> with no arguments. See also <function>IntlGregorianCalendar::__construct<\/function>.",[["$timezone","IntlTimeZone|DateTimeZone|string|null","The timezone to use.\n\n<type>null<\/type>, in which case the default timezone will be used, as specified in the ini setting date.timezone or through the function <function>date_default_timezone_set<\/function> and as returned by <function>date_default_timezone_get<\/function>.\n\nAn <classname>IntlTimeZone<\/classname>, which will be used directly.\n\nA <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname>. Its identifier will be extracted and an ICU timezone object will be created; the timezone will be backed by ICUÊ¼s database, not PHPÊ¼s.\n\nA <type>string<\/type>, which should be a valid ICU timezone identifier. See <function>IntlTimeZone::createTimeZoneIDEnumeration<\/function>. Raw offsets such as <literal>\"GMT+08:30\"<\/literal> are also accepted."],["$locale","string|null","A locale to use or <type>null<\/type> to use the default locale."]],["IntlCalendar|null","The created <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance or <type>null<\/type> on failure."],["IntlGregorianCalendar::__construct"]]
["function","Compare time of two IntlCalendar objects for equality\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns true if this calendar and the given calendar have the same time. The settings, calendar types and field states do not have to be the same.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$other","IntlCalendar","The calendar to compare with the primary object."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the current time of both this and the passed in <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> object are the same, or <type>false<\/type> otherwise.\n\nOn failure <type>false<\/type> is also returned. To detect error conditions use <function>intl_get_error_code<\/function>, or set up Intl to throw exceptions."]]
["function","Calculate difference between given time and this objectÊ¼s time\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturn the difference between the given time and the time this object is set to, with respect to the quantity specified the <parameter>field<\/parameter> parameter.\n\nThis method is meant to be called successively, first with the most significant field of interest down to the least significant field. To this end, as a side effect, this calendarÊ¼s value for the field specified is advanced by the amount returned.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$timestamp","float","The time against which to compare the quantity represented by the <parameter>field<\/parameter>. For the result to be positive, the time given for this parameter must be ahead of the time of the object the method is being invoked on."],["$field","int","The field that represents the quantity being compared.\n\nOne of the <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> date\/time field constants. These are integer values between <literal>0<\/literal> and <constant>IntlCalendar::FIELD_COUNT<\/constant>."]],["int|false","Returns a (signed) difference of time in the unit associated with the specified field or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Create an IntlCalendar from a DateTime object or string\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nCreates an <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> object either from a <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object or from a string from which a <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object can be built.\n\nThe new calendar will represent not only the same instant as the given <classname>DateTime<\/classname> (subject to precision loss for dates very far into the past or future), but also the same timezone (subject to the caveat that different timezone databases will be used, and therefore the results may differ).",[["$datetime","DateTime|string","A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object or a <type>string<\/type> that can be passed to <function>DateTime::__construct<\/function>."]],["IntlCalendar|null","The created <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> object or <type>null<\/type> in case of failure. If a <type>string<\/type> is passed, any exception that occurs inside the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> constructor is propagated."]]
