["function","Get time of the day at which weekend begins or ends\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns the number of milliseconds after midnight at which the weekend begins or ends.\n\nThis is only applicable for days of the week for which <function>IntlCalendar::getDayOfWeekType<\/function> returns either <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_TYPE_WEEKEND_OFFSET<\/constant> or <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_TYPE_WEEKEND_CEASE<\/constant>. Calling this function for other days of the week is an error condition.\n\nThis function requires ICU 4.4 or later.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$dayOfWeek","int","One of the constants <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_SUNDAY<\/constant>, <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_MONDAY<\/constant>, â€¦, <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_SATURDAY<\/constant>."]],["int|false","The number of milliseconds into the day at which the weekend begins or ends or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Whether the objectÊ¼s time is in Daylight Savings Time\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nWhether, for the instant represented by this object and for this objectÊ¼s timezone, daylight saving time is in place.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the date is in Daylight Savings Time, <type>false<\/type> otherwise.\n\nOn failure <type>false<\/type> is also returned. To detect error conditions use <function>intl_get_error_code<\/function>, or set up Intl to throw exceptions."]]
["function","Whether another calendar is equal but for a different time\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns whether this and the given object are equivalent for all purposes except as to the time they have set. The locales do not have to match, as long as no change in behavior results from such mismatch. This includes the timezone, whether the lenient mode is set, the repeated and skipped wall time settings, the days of the week when the weekend starts and ceases and the times where such transitions occur. It may also include other calendar specific settings, such as the Gregorian\/Julian transition instant.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$other","IntlCalendar","The other calendar against which the comparison is to be made."]],["bool","Assuming there are no argument errors, returns <type>true<\/type> if the calendars are equivalent except possibly for their set time."],["IntlCalendar::equals"]]
["function","Whether date\/time interpretation is in lenient mode\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns whether the current date\/time interpretations is lenient (the default). If that is case, some out of range values for fields will be accepted instead of raising an error.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."]],["bool","A <type>bool<\/type> representing whether the calendar is set to lenient mode."]]
["function","Whether a field is set\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns whether a field is set (as opposed to clear). Set fields take priority over unset fields and their default values when the date\/time is being calculated. Fields set later take priority over fields set earlier.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$field","int","One of the <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> date\/time field constants. These are integer values between <literal>0<\/literal> and <constant>IntlCalendar::FIELD_COUNT<\/constant>."]],["bool","Assuming there are no argument errors, returns <type>true<\/type> if the field is set."],["IntlCalendar::clear","IntlCalendar::set"]]
