["function","Set the day on which the week is deemed to start\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nDefines the day of week deemed to start the week. This affects the behavior of fields that depend on the concept of week start and end such as <constant>IntlCalendar::FIELD_WEEK_OF_YEAR<\/constant> and <constant>IntlCalendar::FIELD_YEAR_WOY<\/constant>.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$dayOfWeek","int","One of the constants <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_SUNDAY<\/constant>, <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_MONDAY<\/constant>, â€¦, <constant>IntlCalendar::DOW_SATURDAY<\/constant>."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Set whether date\/time interpretation is to be lenient\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nDefines whether the calendar is â€˜lenient modeâ€™. In such a mode, some of out-of-bounds values for some fields are accepted, the behavior being similar to that of <function>IntlCalendar::add<\/function> (i.e., the value wraps around, carrying into more significant fields each time). If the lenient mode is off, then such values will generate an error.",[["$calendar","IntlCalendar","An <classname>IntlCalendar<\/classname> instance."],["$lenient","bool","Use <type>true<\/type> to activate the lenient mode; <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
