["function","Get the \"age\" of the code point\n\nGets the \"age\" of the code point.\n\nThe \"age\" is the Unicode version when the code point was first designated (as a non-character or for Private Use) or assigned a character. This can be useful to avoid emitting code points to receiving processes that do not accept newer characters.",[["$codepoint","int|string","The <type>int<\/type> codepoint value (e.g. <literal>0x2603<\/literal> for U+2603 SNOWMAN), or the character encoded as a UTF-8 <type>string<\/type> (e.g. <literal>\"\\u{2603}\"<\/literal>)"]],["array|null","The Unicode version number, as an <type>array<\/type>. For example, version 1.3.31.2 would be represented as <literal>[1, 3, 31, 2]<\/literal>. Returns <type>null<\/type> on failure."],["<function>IntlChar::getUnicodeVersion<\/function>","<function>IntlChar::getIntPropertyMinValue<\/function>","<function>IntlChar::getIntPropertyValue<\/function>"]]
