["function","Creates SNMP instance representing session to remote SNMP agent\n\nCreates SNMP instance representing session to remote SNMP agent.",[["$version","int","SNMP protocol version: <constant>SNMP::VERSION_1<\/constant>, <constant>SNMP::VERSION_2C<\/constant>, <constant>SNMP::VERSION_3<\/constant>."],["$hostname","string","The SNMP agent. <parameter>hostname<\/parameter> may be suffixed with optional SNMP agent port after colon. IPv6 addresses must be enclosed in square brackets if used with port. If FQDN is used for <parameter>hostname<\/parameter> it will be resolved by PHP SNMP extension, not by Net-SNMP engine. Usage of IPv6 addresses when specifying FQDN may be forced by enclosing FQDN into square brackets. Here are some examples: IPv4 with default port127.0.0.1IPv6 with default port::1 or [::1]IPv4 with specific port127.0.0.1:1161IPv6 with specific port[::1]:1161FQDN with default porthost.domainFQDN with specific porthost.domain:1161FQDN with default port, force usage of IPv6 address[host.domain]FQDN with specific port, force usage of IPv6 address[host.domain]:1161"],["$community","string","Specifies the security level for given <parameter>version<\/parameter>. The purpose of <parameter>community<\/parameter> access string is SNMP version specific:\n\nSNMPv3 requires to configure security-related session parameters with the SNMP::setSecurity method."],["$timeout","int","The number of microseconds until the first timeout."],["$retries","int","The number of retries in case timeout occurs."]],null,["SNMP::close"]]
