["function","Fetch SNMP object subtree\n\nSNMP::walk is used to read SNMP subtree rooted at specified <parameter>objectId<\/parameter>.",[["$objectId","array|string","Root of subtree to be fetched"],["$suffixAsKey","bool","By default full OID notation is used for keys in output array. If set to <type>true<\/type> subtree prefix will be removed from keys leaving only suffix of object_id."],["$nonRepeaters","int","This specifies the number of supplied variables that should not be iterated over. The default is to use this value from SNMP object."],["$maxRepetitions","int","This specifies the maximum number of iterations over the repeating variables. The default is to use this value from SNMP object."]],["array|false","Returns an associative array of the SNMP object ids and their values on success or <type>false<\/type> on error. When a SNMP error occures SNMP::getErrno and SNMP::getError can be used for retrieving error number (specific to SNMP extension, see class constants) and error message respectively."],["SNMP::getErrno","SNMP::getError"]]
