["function","Opens a stream resource to read a BLOB\n\nOpens a stream resource to read or write a BLOB, which would be selected by:\n\nSELECT <parameter>column<\/parameter> FROM <parameter>database<\/parameter>.<parameter>table<\/parameter> WHERE rowid = <parameter>rowid<\/parameter>\n\nIt is not possible to change the size of a BLOB by writing to the stream. Instead, an UPDATE statement has to be executed, possibly using SQLite's zeroblob() function to set the desired BLOB size.",[["$table","string","The table name."],["$column","string","The column name."],["$rowid","int","The row ID."],["$database","string","The symbolic name of the DB"],["$flags","int","Either <constant>SQLITE3_OPEN_READONLY<\/constant> or  <constant>SQLITE3_OPEN_READWRITE<\/constant> to open the stream for reading only, or for reading and writing, respectively."]],["resource|false","Returns a stream resource,  or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
