h angle = 102Â°). It starts at <literal>civil_twilight_end<\/literal>.\n\nThe start of the astronomical dawn (zenith angle = 108Â°). It ends at <literal>nautical_twilight_begin<\/literal>.\n\nThe end of the astronomical dusk (zenith angle = 108Â°). It starts at <literal>nautical_twilight_end<\/literal>.\n\nThe values of the array elements are either UNIX timestamps, <type>false<\/type> if the sun is below the respective zenith for the whole day, or <type>true<\/type> if the sun is above the respective zenith for the whole day."]]
["function","Returns time of sunrise for a given day and location\n\n<function>date_sunrise<\/function> returns the sunrise time for a given day (specified as a <parameter>timestamp<\/parameter>) and location.",[["$timestamp","int","The <parameter>timestamp<\/parameter> of the day from which the sunrise time is taken."],["$returnFormat","int","<parameter>returnFormat<\/parameter> constantsconstantdescriptionexampleSUNFUNCS_RET_STRINGreturns the result as <type>string<\/type>16:46SUNFUNCS_RET_DOUBLEreturns the result as <type>float<\/type>16.78243132SUNFUNCS_RET_TIMESTAMPreturns the result as <type>int<\/type> (timestamp)1095034606"],["$latitude","float|null","Defaults to North, pass in a negative value for South. See also: date.default_latitude"],["$longitude","float|null","Defaults to East, pass in a negative value for West. See also: date.default_longitude"],["$zenith","float|null","<parameter>zenith<\/parameter> is the angle between the center of the sun and a line perpendicular to earth's surface. It defaults to date.sunrise_zenith Common <parameter>zenith<\/parameter> anglesAngleDescription90Â°50'Sunrise: the point where the sun becomes visible.96Â°Civil twilight: conventionally used to signify the start of dawn.102Â°Nautical twilight: the point at which the horizon starts being visible at sea.108Â°Astronomical twilight: the point at which the sun starts being the source of any illumination."],["$utcOffset","float|null","Specified in hours. The <parameter>utcOffset<\/parameter> is ignored, if <parameter>returnFormat<\/parameter> is <constant>SUNFUNCS_RET_TIMESTAMP<\/constant>."]],["string|int|float|false","Returns the sunrise time in a specified <parameter>returnFormat<\/parameter> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure. One potential reason for failure is that the sun does not rise at all, which happens inside the polar circles for part of the year."],["<function>date_sun_info<\/function>"]]
