["function","Retrieves a file from the FTP server and writes it to a local file (non-blocking)\n\n<function>ftp_nb_get<\/function> retrieves a remote file from the FTP server, and saves it into a local file.\n\nThe difference between this function and <function>ftp_get<\/function> is that this function retrieves the file asynchronously, so your program can perform  other operations while the file is being downloaded.",[["$ftp","FTP\\Connection","An <classname>FTP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$local_filename","string","The local file path (will be overwritten if the file already exists)."],["$remote_filename","string","The remote file path."],["$mode","int","The transfer mode. Must be either <constant>FTP_ASCII<\/constant> or <constant>FTP_BINARY<\/constant>."],["$offset","int","The position in the remote file to start downloading from."]],["int|false","Returns <constant>FTP_FAILED<\/constant> or <constant>FTP_FINISHED<\/constant> or <constant>FTP_MOREDATA<\/constant>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure to open the local file."],["<function>ftp_nb_fget<\/function>","<function>ftp_nb_continue<\/function>","<function>ftp_fget<\/function>","<function>ftp_get<\/function>"]]
["function","Stores a file on the FTP server (non-blocking)\n\n<function>ftp_nb_put<\/function> stores a local file on the FTP server.\n\nThe difference between this function and the <function>ftp_put<\/function> is that this function uploads the file asynchronously, so your program can perform other operations while the file is being uploaded.",[["$ftp","FTP\\Connection","An <classname>FTP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$remote_filename","string","The remote file path."],["$local_filename","string","The local file path."],["$mode","int","The transfer mode. Must be either <constant>FTP_ASCII<\/constant> or <constant>FTP_BINARY<\/constant>."],["$offset","int","The position in the remote file to start uploading to."]],["int|false","Returns <constant>FTP_FAILED<\/constant> or <constant>FTP_FINISHED<\/constant> or <constant>FTP_MOREDATA<\/constant>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure to open the local file."],["<function>ftp_nb_fput<\/function>","<function>ftp_nb_continue<\/function>","<function>ftp_put<\/function>","<function>ftp_fput<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns a list of files in the given directory",[["$ftp","FTP\\Connection","An <classname>FTP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$directory","string","The directory to be listed. This parameter can also include arguments, eg. <literal>ftp_nlist($ftp, \"-la \/your\/dir\");<\/literal>. Note that this parameter isn't escaped so there may be some issues with filenames containing spaces and other characters."]],["array|false","Returns an array of filenames from the specified directory on success or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>ftp_rawlist<\/function>","<function>ftp_mlsd<\/function>"]]
["function","Turns passive mode on or off\n\n<function>ftp_pasv<\/function> turns on or off passive mode. In passive mode, data connections are initiated by the client, rather than by the server. It may be needed if the client is behind firewall.\n\nPlease note that <function>ftp_pasv<\/function> can only be called after a successful login or otherwise it will fail.",[["$ftp","FTP\\Connection","An <classname>FTP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$enable","bool","If <type>true<\/type>, the passive mode is turned on, else it's turned off."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
