["function","Returns a detailed list of files in the given directory\n\n<function>ftp_rawlist<\/function> executes the FTP  LIST command, and returns the result as an array.",[["$ftp","FTP\\Connection","An <classname>FTP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$directory","string","The directory path. May include arguments for the LIST command."],["$recursive","bool","If set to <type>true<\/type>, the issued command will be LIST -R."]],["array|false","Returns an array where each element corresponds to one line of text. Returns <type>false<\/type> when passed <parameter>directory<\/parameter> is invalid.\n\nThe output is not parsed in any way. The system type identifier returned by <function>ftp_systype<\/function> can be used to determine how the results  should be interpreted."],["<function>ftp_nlist<\/function>","<function>ftp_mlsd<\/function>"]]
["function","Renames a file or a directory on the FTP server\n\n<function>ftp_rename<\/function> renames a file or a directory on the FTP server.",[["$ftp","FTP\\Connection","An <classname>FTP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$from","string","The old file\/directory name."],["$to","string","The new name."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure. Upon failure (such as attempting to rename a non-existent file), an <constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> error will be emitted."]]
