["function","Syntax highlighting of a file\n\nPrints out or returns a syntax highlighted version of the code contained in <parameter>filename<\/parameter> using the colors defined in the built-in syntax highlighter for PHP.\n\nMany servers are configured to automatically highlight files with a phps extension. For example, example.phps when viewed will show the syntax highlighted source of the file. To enable this, add this line to the httpd.conf:",[["$filename","string","Path to the PHP file to be highlighted."],["$return","bool","Set this parameter to <type>true<\/type> to make this function return the highlighted code."]],["string|bool","If <parameter>return<\/parameter> is set to <type>true<\/type>, returns the highlighted code as a string instead of printing it out. Otherwise, it will return <type>true<\/type> on success, <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>highlight_string<\/function>","Highlighting INI directives"]]
