["function","Check current mailbox\n\nChecks information about the current mailbox.",[["$imap","IMAP\\Connection","An <classname>IMAP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."]],["stdClass|false","Returns the information in an object with following properties: <constant>Date<\/constant> - current system time formatted according to RFC2822 <constant>Driver<\/constant> - protocol used to access this mailbox: POP3, IMAP, NNTP <constant>Mailbox<\/constant> - the mailbox name <constant>Nmsgs<\/constant> - number of messages in the mailbox <constant>Recent<\/constant> - number of recent messages in the mailbox \n\n<constant>Date<\/constant> - current system time formatted according to RFC2822\n\n<constant>Driver<\/constant> - protocol used to access this mailbox: POP3, IMAP, NNTP\n\n<constant>Mailbox<\/constant> - the mailbox name\n\n<constant>Nmsgs<\/constant> - number of messages in the mailbox\n\n<constant>Recent<\/constant> - number of recent messages in the mailbox\n\nReturns <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Clears flags on messages\n\nThis function causes a store to delete the specified <parameter>flag<\/parameter> to the flags set for the messages in the specified <parameter>sequence<\/parameter>.",[["$imap","IMAP\\Connection","An <classname>IMAP\\Connection<\/classname> instance."],["$sequence","string","A sequence of message numbers. You can enumerate desired messages with the <literal>X,Y<\/literal> syntax, or retrieve all messages  within an interval with the <literal>X:Y<\/literal> syntax"],["$flag","string","The flags which you can unset are \"\\\\Seen\", \"\\\\Answered\", \"\\\\Flagged\", \"\\\\Deleted\", and \"\\\\Draft\" (as defined by RFC2060)"],["$options","int","<parameter>options<\/parameter> are a bit mask and may contain the single option: <constant>ST_UID<\/constant> - The sequence argument contains UIDs instead of sequence numbers \n\n<constant>ST_UID<\/constant> - The sequence argument contains UIDs instead of sequence numbers"]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."],["<function>imap_setflag_full<\/function>"]]
