["function","Performs an extended operation\n\nPerforms an extended operation on the specified <parameter>ldap<\/parameter> with <parameter>request_oid<\/parameter> the OID of the operation and <parameter>request_data<\/parameter> the data.",[["$ldap","LDAP\\Connection","An <classname>LDAP\\Connection<\/classname> instance, returned by <function>ldap_connect<\/function>."],["$request_oid","string","The extended operation request OID. You may use one of <constant>LDAP_EXOP_START_TLS<\/constant>, <constant>LDAP_EXOP_MODIFY_PASSWD<\/constant>, <constant>LDAP_EXOP_REFRESH<\/constant>, <constant>LDAP_EXOP_WHO_AM_I<\/constant>, <constant>LDAP_EXOP_TURN<\/constant>, or a string with the OID of the operation you want to send."],["$request_data","string","The extended operation request data. May be NULL for some operations like <constant>LDAP_EXOP_WHO_AM_I<\/constant>, may also need to be BER encoded."],["$controls","array","Array of LDAP Controls to send with the request."],["$response_data","string","Will be filled with the extended operation response data if provided. If not provided you may use ldap_parse_exop on the result object later to get this data."],["$response_oid","string","Will be filled with the response OID if provided, usually equal to the request OID."]],["mixed","When used with <parameter>response_data<\/parameter>, returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on error. When used without <parameter>response_data<\/parameter>, returns a result identifier or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>ldap_parse_result<\/function>","<function>ldap_parse_exop<\/function>","<function>ldap_exop_whoami<\/function>","<function>ldap_exop_refresh<\/function>","<function>ldap_exop_passwd<\/function>"]]
