["function","Get information about the most recent query\n\nReturns detailed information about the last query.",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["string","Returns information about the statement on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure. See the example below for which statements provide information, and what the returned value may look like. Statements that are not listed will return <type>false<\/type>."],["<function>mysql_affected_rows<\/function>","<function>mysql_insert_id<\/function>","<function>mysql_stat<\/function>"]]
["function","Get the ID generated in the last query\n\nRetrieves the ID generated for an AUTO_INCREMENT column by the previous query (usually INSERT).",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["int","The ID generated for an AUTO_INCREMENT column by the previous query on success, <literal>0<\/literal> if the previous query does not generate an AUTO_INCREMENT value, or <type>false<\/type> if no MySQL connection was established."],["<function>mysql_query<\/function>","<function>mysql_info<\/function>"]]
["function","List databases available on a MySQL server\n\nReturns a result pointer containing the databases available from the current mysql daemon.",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["resource","Returns a result pointer <type>resource<\/type> on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure. Use the <function>mysql_tablename<\/function> function to traverse this result pointer, or any function for result tables, such as <function>mysql_fetch_array<\/function>."],["<function>mysql_db_name<\/function>","<function>mysql_select_db<\/function>"]]
["function","List MySQL table fields\n\nRetrieves information about the given table name.\n\nThis function is deprecated. It is preferable to use <function>mysql_query<\/function> to issue an SQL <literal>SHOW COLUMNS FROM table [LIKE 'name']<\/literal> statement instead.",[["$database_name","string","The name of the database that's being queried."],["$table_name","string","The name of the table that's being queried."],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["resource","A result pointer <type>resource<\/type> on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe returned result can be used with <function>mysql_field_flags<\/function>, <function>mysql_field_len<\/function>, <function>mysql_field_name<\/function> and <function>mysql_field_type<\/function>."],["<function>mysql_field_flags<\/function>","<function>mysql_info<\/function>"]]
["function","List MySQL processes\n\nRetrieves the current MySQL server threads.",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["resource|false","A result pointer <type>resource<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_thread_id<\/function>","<function>mysql_stat<\/function>"]]
["function","List tables in a MySQL database\n\nRetrieves a list of table names from a MySQL database.\n\nThis function is deprecated. It is preferable to use <function>mysql_query<\/function> to issue an SQL <literal>SHOW TABLES [FROM db_name] [LIKE 'pattern']<\/literal> statement instead.",[["$database","string","The name of the database"],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["resource|false","A result pointer <type>resource<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nUse the <function>mysql_tablename<\/function> function to traverse this result pointer, or any function for result tables, such as <function>mysql_fetch_array<\/function>."],["<function>mysql_list_dbs<\/function>","<function>mysql_tablename<\/function>"]]
["function","Get number of fields in result\n\nRetrieves the number of fields from a query.",[["$result","resource","The result <type>resource<\/type> that\nis being evaluated. This result comes from a call to\n<function>mysql_query<\/function>."]],["int|false","Returns the number of fields in the result set <type>resource<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_select_db<\/function>","<function>mysql_query<\/function>","<function>mysql_fetch_field<\/function>","<function>mysql_num_rows<\/function>"]]
["function","Get number of rows in result\n\nRetrieves the number of rows from a result set. This command is only valid for statements like SELECT or SHOW that return an actual result set. To retrieve the number of rows affected by a INSERT, UPDATE, REPLACE or DELETE query, use <function>mysql_affected_rows<\/function>.",[["$result","resource","The result <type>resource<\/type> that\nis being evaluated. This result comes from a call to\n<function>mysql_query<\/function>."]],["int|false","The number of rows in a result set on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_affected_rows<\/function>","<function>mysql_connect<\/function>","<function>mysql_data_seek<\/function>","<function>mysql_select_db<\/function>","<function>mysql_query<\/function>"]]
["function","Open a persistent connection to a MySQL server\n\nEstablishes a persistent connection to a MySQL server.\n\n<function>mysql_pconnect<\/function> acts very much like <function>mysql_connect<\/function> with two major differences.\n\nFirst, when connecting, the function would first try to find a (persistent) link that's already open with the same host, username and password.  If one is found, an identifier for it will be returned instead of opening a new connection.\n\nSecond, the connection to the SQL server will not be closed when the execution of the script ends.  Instead, the link will remain open for future use (<function>mysql_close<\/function> will not close links established by <function>mysql_pconnect<\/function>).\n\nThis type of link is therefore called 'persistent'.",[["$server","string","The MySQL server. It can also include a port number. e.g. \"hostname:port\" or a path to a local socket e.g. \":\/path\/to\/socket\" for the localhost.\n\nIf the PHP directive  mysql.default_host is undefined (default), then the default value is 'localhost:3306'"],["$username","string","The username. Default value is the name of the user that owns the server process."],["$password","string","The password. Default value is an empty password."],["$client_flags","int","The <parameter>client_flags<\/parameter> parameter can be a combination of the following constants: 128 (enable <literal>LOAD DATA LOCAL<\/literal> handling), <constant>MYSQL_CLIENT_SSL<\/constant>, <constant>MYSQL_CLIENT_COMPRESS<\/constant>, <constant>MYSQL_CLIENT_IGNORE_SPACE<\/constant> or <constant>MYSQL_CLIENT_INTERACTIVE<\/constant>."]],["resource","Returns a MySQL persistent link identifier on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_connect<\/function>","Persistent\n   Database Connections"]]
["function","Ping a server connection or reconnect if there is no connection\n\nChecks whether or not the connection to the server is working. If it has gone down, an automatic reconnection is attempted. This function can be used by scripts that remain idle for a long while, to check whether or not the server has closed the connection and reconnect if necessary.\n\nAutomatic reconnection is disabled by default in versions of MySQL >= 5.0.3.",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the connection to the server MySQL server is working, otherwise <type>false<\/type>."],["<function>mysql_thread_id<\/function>","<function>mysql_list_processes<\/function>"]]
["function","Send a MySQL query\n\n<function>mysql_query<\/function> sends a unique query (multiple queries are not supported) to the currently active database on the server that's associated with the specified <parameter>link_identifier<\/parameter>.",[["$query","string","An SQL query\n\nThe query string should not end with a semicolon. Data inside the query should be properly escaped."],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["mixed","For SELECT, SHOW, DESCRIBE, EXPLAIN and other statements returning resultset, <function>mysql_query<\/function> returns a <type>resource<\/type> on success, or <type>false<\/type> on error.\n\nFor other type of SQL statements, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, etc, <function>mysql_query<\/function> returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on error.\n\nThe returned result resource should be passed to <function>mysql_fetch_array<\/function>, and other functions for dealing with result tables, to access the returned data.\n\nUse <function>mysql_num_rows<\/function> to find out how many rows were returned for a SELECT statement or <function>mysql_affected_rows<\/function> to find out how many rows were affected by a DELETE, INSERT, REPLACE, or UPDATE statement.\n\n<function>mysql_query<\/function> will also fail and return <type>false<\/type> if the user does not have permission to access the table(s) referenced by the query."],["<function>mysql_connect<\/function>","<function>mysql_error<\/function>","<function>mysql_real_escape_string<\/function>","<function>mysql_result<\/function>","<function>mysql_fetch_assoc<\/function>","<function>mysql_unbuffered_query<\/function>"]]
["function","Escapes special characters in a string for use in an SQL statement\n\nEscapes special characters in the <parameter>unescaped_string<\/parameter>, taking into account the current character set of the connection so that it is safe to place it in a <function>mysql_query<\/function>. If binary data is to be inserted, this function must be used.\n\n<function>mysql_real_escape_string<\/function> calls MySQL's library function mysql_real_escape_string, which prepends backslashes to the following characters: <literal>\\x00<\/literal>, <literal>\\n<\/literal>, <literal>\\r<\/literal>, <literal>\\<\/literal>, <literal>'<\/literal>, <literal>\"<\/literal> and <literal>\\x1a<\/literal>.\n\nThis function must always (with few exceptions) be used to make data safe before sending a query to MySQL.\n\nThe character set must be set either at the server level, or with the API function <function>mysql_set_charset<\/function> for it to affect <function>mysql_real_escape_string<\/function>. See the concepts section on character sets for more information.",[["$unescaped_string","string","The string that is to be escaped."],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["string","Returns the escaped string, or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>mysql_set_charset<\/function>","<function>mysql_client_encoding<\/function>"]]
["function","Get result data\n\nRetrieves the contents of one cell from a MySQL result set.\n\nWhen working on large result sets, you should consider using one of the functions that fetch an entire row (specified below).  As these functions return the contents of multiple cells in one function call, they're MUCH quicker than <function>mysql_result<\/function>.  Also, note that specifying a numeric offset for the field argument is much quicker than specifying a fieldname or tablename.fieldname argument.",[["$result","resource","The result <type>resource<\/type> that\nis being evaluated. This result comes from a call to\n<function>mysql_query<\/function>."],["$row","int","The row number from the result that's being retrieved. Row numbers start at <literal>0<\/literal>."],["$field","mixed","The name or offset of the field being retrieved.\n\nIt can be the field's offset, the field's name, or the field's table dot field name (tablename.fieldname). If the column name has been aliased ('select foo as bar from...'), use the alias instead of the column name. If undefined, the first field is retrieved."]],["string","The contents of one cell from a MySQL result set on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_fetch_row<\/function>","<function>mysql_fetch_array<\/function>","<function>mysql_fetch_assoc<\/function>","<function>mysql_fetch_object<\/function>"]]
["function","Select a MySQL database\n\nSets the current active database on the server that's associated with the specified link identifier. Every subsequent call to <function>mysql_query<\/function> will be made on the active database.",[["$database_name","string","The name of the database that is to be selected."],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_connect<\/function>","<function>mysql_pconnect<\/function>","<function>mysql_query<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the client character set\n\nSets the default character set for the current connection.",[["$charset","string","A valid character set name."],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["Setting character sets in MySQL","List of character sets that MySQL supports","<function>mysql_client_encoding<\/function>"]]
["function","Get current system status\n\n<function>mysql_stat<\/function> returns the current server status.",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["string","Returns a string with the status for uptime, threads, queries, open tables, flush tables and queries per second. For a complete list of other status variables, you have to use the <literal>SHOW STATUS<\/literal> SQL command. If <parameter>link_identifier<\/parameter> is invalid, <type>null<\/type> is returned."],["<function>mysql_get_server_info<\/function>","<function>mysql_list_processes<\/function>"]]
["function","Get table name of field\n\nRetrieves the table name from a <parameter>result<\/parameter>.\n\nThis function is deprecated. It is preferable to use <function>mysql_query<\/function> to issue an SQL <literal>SHOW TABLES [FROM db_name] [LIKE 'pattern']<\/literal> statement instead.",[["$result","resource","A result pointer <type>resource<\/type> that's returned from <function>mysql_list_tables<\/function>."],["$i","int","The integer index (row\/table number)"]],["string|false","The name of the table on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nUse the <function>mysql_tablename<\/function> function to traverse this result pointer, or any function for result tables, such as <function>mysql_fetch_array<\/function>."],["<function>mysql_list_tables<\/function>","<function>mysql_field_table<\/function>","<function>mysql_db_name<\/function>"]]
["function","Return the current thread ID\n\nRetrieves the current thread ID. If the connection is lost, and a reconnect with <function>mysql_ping<\/function> is executed, the thread ID will change. This means only retrieve the thread ID when needed.",[["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["int|false","The thread ID on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysql_ping<\/function>","<function>mysql_list_processes<\/function>"]]
["function","Send an SQL query to MySQL without fetching and buffering the result rows\n\n<function>mysql_unbuffered_query<\/function> sends the SQL query <parameter>query<\/parameter> to MySQL without automatically fetching and buffering the result rows as <function>mysql_query<\/function> does.  This saves a considerable amount of memory with SQL queries that produce large result sets, and you can start working on the result set immediately after the first row has been retrieved as you don't have to wait until the complete SQL query has been performed.  To use <function>mysql_unbuffered_query<\/function> while multiple database connections are open, you must specify the optional parameter <parameter>link_identifier<\/parameter> to identify which connection you want to use.",[["$query","string","The SQL query to execute.\n\nData inside the query should be properly escaped."],["$link_identifier","resource","The MySQL connection. If the\nlink identifier is not specified, the last link opened by\n<function>mysql_connect<\/function> is assumed. If no such link is found, it\nwill try to create one as if <function>mysql_connect<\/function> had been called\nwith no arguments. If no connection is found or established, an\n<constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> level error is generated."]],["resource","For SELECT, SHOW, DESCRIBE or EXPLAIN statements, <function>mysql_unbuffered_query<\/function> returns a <type>resource<\/type> on success, or <type>false<\/type> on error.\n\nFor other type of SQL statements, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, etc, <function>mysql_unbuffered_query<\/function> returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>mysql_query<\/function>"]]
["function","Close client\n\nClose all client connections with the server.",null,["bool","<type>true<\/type> if connections are closed."]]
["function","Open a new connection to the MySQL server\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nOpens a connection to the MySQL Server.",[["$hostname","string|null","Can be either a host name or an IP address. When passing <type>null<\/type>, the value is retrieved from mysqli.default_host. When possible, pipes will be used instead of the TCP\/IP protocol. The TCP\/IP protocol is used if a host name and port number are provided together e.g. <literal>localhost:3308<\/literal>.\n\nPrepending host by <literal>p:<\/literal> opens a persistent connection. <function>mysqli_change_user<\/function> is automatically called on connections opened from the connection pool."],["$username","string|null","The MySQL username or <type>null<\/type> to assume the username based on the mysqli.default_user ini option."],["$password","string|null","The MySQL password or <type>null<\/type> to assume the password based on the mysqli.default_pw ini option."],["$database","string|null","The default database to be used when performing queries or <type>null<\/type>."],["$port","int|null","The port number to attempt to connect to the MySQL server or <type>null<\/type> to assume the port based on the mysqli.default_port ini option."],["$socket","string|null","The socket or named pipe that should be used or <type>null<\/type> to assume the socket based on the mysqli.default_socket ini option.\n\nSpecifying the <parameter>socket<\/parameter> parameter will not explicitly determine the type of connection to be used when connecting to the MySQL server. How the connection is made to the MySQL database is determined by the <parameter>hostname<\/parameter> parameter."]],["bool","mysqli::__construct always returns an object which represents the connection to a MySQL Server, regardless of it being successful or not.\n\n<function>mysqli_connect<\/function> returns an object which represents the connection to a MySQL Server, or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nmysqli::connect returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure. Prior to PHP 8.1.0, returns <type>null<\/type> on success."],["<function>mysqli_real_connect<\/function>","<function>mysqli_options<\/function>","<function>mysqli_connect_errno<\/function>","<function>mysqli_connect_error<\/function>","<function>mysqli_close<\/function>"]]
["function","Turns on or off auto-committing database modifications\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nTurns on or off auto-commit mode on queries for the database connection.\n\nTo determine the current state of autocommit use the SQL command <literal>SELECT @@autocommit<\/literal>.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"],["$enable","bool","Whether to turn on auto-commit or not."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysqli_begin_transaction<\/function>","<function>mysqli_commit<\/function>","<function>mysqli_rollback<\/function>"]]
["function","Starts a transaction\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style:\n\nBegins a transaction. Requires the InnoDB  engine (it is enabled by default). For additional details about how MySQL transactions work, see http:\/\/dev.mysql.com\/doc\/mysql\/en\/commit.html.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"],["$flags","int","Valid flags are:\n\n<constant>MYSQLI_TRANS_START_READ_ONLY<\/constant>:  Start the transaction as \"START TRANSACTION READ ONLY\". Requires MySQL 5.6 and above.\n\n<constant>MYSQLI_TRANS_START_READ_WRITE<\/constant>:  Start the transaction as \"START TRANSACTION READ WRITE\". Requires MySQL 5.6 and above.\n\n<constant>MYSQLI_TRANS_START_WITH_CONSISTENT_SNAPSHOT<\/constant>:  Start the transaction as \"START TRANSACTION WITH CONSISTENT SNAPSHOT\"."],["$name","string|null","Savepoint name for the transaction."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysqli_autocommit<\/function>","<function>mysqli_commit<\/function>","<function>mysqli_rollback<\/function>"]]
["function","Changes the user of the database connection\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nAttempts to connect to the specified database using the provided credentials.\n\nIn comparison to mysqli::connect, this method will not disconnect the current connection if the new connection cannot be opened.\n\nIn order to successfully change users a valid <parameter>username<\/parameter> and <parameter>password<\/parameter> parameters must be provided and that user must have sufficient permissions to access the desired database. If for any reason authorization fails, the current user authentication will remain.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"],["$username","string","The MySQL user name."],["$password","string","The MySQL password."],["$database","string|null","The database name. If <type>null<\/type> or an empty string is passed, the connection to the server will be opened with no default database."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysqli_connect<\/function>","<function>mysqli_select_db<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns the current character set of the database connection\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns the current character set of the database connection.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"]],["string","The current character set of the connection"],["<function>mysqli_set_charset<\/function>","<function>mysqli_real_escape_string<\/function>"]]
["function","Closes a previously opened database connection\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nCloses a previously opened database connection.\n\nOpen non-persistent MySQL connections and result sets are automatically closed when their objects are destroyed. Explicitly closing open  connections and freeing result sets is optional. However, it's a good idea to close the connection as soon as the script finishes performing all of its database operations, if it still has a lot of processing to do after getting the results.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."],["mysqli::__construct","<function>mysqli_init<\/function>","<function>mysqli_real_connect<\/function>","<function>mysqli_free_result<\/function>"]]
["function","Commits the current transaction\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nCommits the current transaction for the database connection.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"],["$flags","int","A bitmask of <constant>MYSQLI_TRANS_COR_*<\/constant> constants."],["$name","string|null","If provided then <literal>COMMIT\/*name*\/<\/literal> is executed."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysqli_autocommit<\/function>","<function>mysqli_begin_transaction<\/function>","<function>mysqli_rollback<\/function>","<function>mysqli_savepoint<\/function>"]]
["function","Open a new connection to the MySQL server\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nOpens a connection to the MySQL Server.",[["$hostname","string|null","Can be either a host name or an IP address. When passing <type>null<\/type>, the value is retrieved from mysqli.default_host. When possible, pipes will be used instead of the TCP\/IP protocol. The TCP\/IP protocol is used if a host name and port number are provided together e.g. <literal>localhost:3308<\/literal>.\n\nPrepending host by <literal>p:<\/literal> opens a persistent connection. <function>mysqli_change_user<\/function> is automatically called on connections opened from the connection pool."],["$username","string|null","The MySQL username or <type>null<\/type> to assume the username based on the mysqli.default_user ini option."],["$password","string|null","The MySQL password or <type>null<\/type> to assume the password based on the mysqli.default_pw ini option."],["$database","string|null","The default database to be used when performing queries or <type>null<\/type>."],["$port","int|null","The port number to attempt to connect to the MySQL server or <type>null<\/type> to assume the port based on the mysqli.default_port ini option."],["$socket","string|null","The socket or named pipe that should be used or <type>null<\/type> to assume the socket based on the mysqli.default_socket ini option.\n\nSpecifying the <parameter>socket<\/parameter> parameter will not explicitly determine the type of connection to be used when connecting to the MySQL server. How the connection is made to the MySQL database is determined by the <parameter>hostname<\/parameter> parameter."]],["bool","mysqli::__construct always returns an object which represents the connection to a MySQL Server, regardless of it being successful or not.\n\n<function>mysqli_connect<\/function> returns an object which represents the connection to a MySQL Server, or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nmysqli::connect returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure. Prior to PHP 8.1.0, returns <type>null<\/type> on success."],["<function>mysqli_real_connect<\/function>","<function>mysqli_options<\/function>","<function>mysqli_connect_errno<\/function>","<function>mysqli_connect_error<\/function>","<function>mysqli_close<\/function>"]]
["function","Performs debugging operations\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nPerforms debugging operations using the Fred Fish debugging library.",[["$options","string","A string representing the debugging operation to perform\n\nThe debug control string is a sequence of colon separated fields as follows: <literal>::]]><\/literal> Each field consists of a mandatory flag character followed by an optional <literal>,<\/literal> and comma separated list of modifiers: <literal>flag[,modifier,modifier,...,modifier]<\/literal>\n\nRecognized Flag Characters<parameter>options<\/parameter> characterDescriptionO<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_FLUSH<\/constant>A\/a<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_APPEND<\/constant>F<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_DUMP_FILE<\/constant>i<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_DUMP_PID<\/constant>L<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_DUMP_LINE<\/constant>m<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_TRACE_MEMORY_CALLS<\/constant>n<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_DUMP_LEVEL<\/constant>ooutput to fileT<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_DUMP_TIME<\/constant>t<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_DUMP_TRACE<\/constant>x<constant>MYSQLND_DEBUG_PROFILE_CALLS<\/constant>"]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."],["<function>mysqli_dump_debug_info<\/function>","<function>mysqli_report<\/function>"]]
["function","Dump debugging information into the log\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nThis function is designed to be executed by an user with the SUPER privilege and is used to dump debugging information into the log for the MySQL Server relating to the connection.",[["$mysql","mysqli","Procedural style only: A <classname>mysqli<\/classname> object\nreturned by <function>mysqli_connect<\/function> or <function>mysqli_init<\/function>"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>mysqli_debug<\/function>"]]
