["function","Lists columns and associated privileges for the given table\n\nLists columns and associated privileges for the given table.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object,\nsee <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$table","string","The table name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$column","string","The column name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure. This result object can be used to fetch a list of columns and associated privileges.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>GRANTOR<\/literal><literal>GRANTEE<\/literal><literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal><literal>IS_GRANTABLE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\n<literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>\n\n<literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>\n\n<literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal>\n\n<literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal>\n\n<literal>GRANTOR<\/literal>\n\n<literal>GRANTEE<\/literal>\n\n<literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal>\n\n<literal>IS_GRANTABLE<\/literal>\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal>, <literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal>."]]
["function","Lists the column names in specified tables\n\nLists all columns in the requested range.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object,\nsee <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string|null","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$table","string|null","The table name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$column","string|null","The column name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>TYPE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_SIZE<\/literal><literal>BUFFER_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>DECIMAL_DIGITS<\/literal><literal>NUM_PREC_RADIX<\/literal><literal>NULLABLE<\/literal><literal>REMARKS<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_DEF<\/literal><literal>SQL_DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>SQL_DATETIME_SUB<\/literal><literal>CHAR_OCTET_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal><literal>IS_NULLABLE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\n<literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>\n\n<literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>\n\n<literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal>\n\n<literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal>\n\n<literal>DATA_TYPE<\/literal>\n\n<literal>TYPE_NAME<\/literal>\n\n<literal>COLUMN_SIZE<\/literal>\n\n<literal>BUFFER_LENGTH<\/literal>\n\n<literal>DECIMAL_DIGITS<\/literal>\n\n<literal>NUM_PREC_RADIX<\/literal>\n\n<literal>NULLABLE<\/literal>\n\n<literal>REMARKS<\/literal>\n\n<literal>COLUMN_DEF<\/literal>\n\n<literal>SQL_DATA_TYPE<\/literal>\n\n<literal>SQL_DATETIME_SUB<\/literal>\n\n<literal>CHAR_OCTET_LENGTH<\/literal>\n\n<literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal>\n\n<literal>IS_NULLABLE<\/literal>\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_columnprivileges<\/function>","<function>odbc_procedurecolumns<\/function>"]]
