["function","Get the list of procedures stored in a specific data source\n\nLists all procedures in the requested range.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object,\nsee <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string|null","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$procedure","string|null","The name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns:\n<literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters,\nand <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object containing the information or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal><literal>NUM_INPUT_PARAMS<\/literal><literal>NUM_OUTPUT_PARAMS<\/literal><literal>NUM_RESULT_SETS<\/literal><literal>REMARKS<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_TYPE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\n<literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal>\n\n<literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEM<\/literal>\n\n<literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal>\n\n<literal>NUM_INPUT_PARAMS<\/literal>\n\n<literal>NUM_OUTPUT_PARAMS<\/literal>\n\n<literal>NUM_RESULT_SETS<\/literal>\n\n<literal>REMARKS<\/literal>\n\n<literal>PROCEDURE_TYPE<\/literal>\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEMA<\/literal> and <literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_procedurecolumns<\/function>","<function>odbc_tables<\/function>"]]
