["function","Open sealed data\n\n<function>openssl_open<\/function> opens (decrypts) <parameter>data<\/parameter> using an envelope key that is decrypted from <parameter>encrypted_key<\/parameter> using <parameter>private_key<\/parameter>. The decryption is done using <parameter>cipher_algo<\/parameter> and <parameter>iv<\/parameter>. The IV is required only if the cipher method requires it. The function fills <parameter>output<\/parameter> with the decrypted data. The envelope key is usually generated when the data are sealed using a public key that is associated with the private key. See <function>openssl_seal<\/function> for more information.",[["$data","string","The sealed data."],["$output","string","If the call is successful the opened data is returned in this parameter."],["$encrypted_key","string","The encrypted symmetric key that can be decrypted using <parameter>private_key<\/parameter>."],["$private_key","OpenSSLAsymmetricKey|OpenSSLCertificate|array|string","The private key used for decrypting <parameter>encrypted_key<\/parameter>."],["$cipher_algo","string","The cipher method used for decryption of <parameter>data<\/parameter>.  The default value for PHP versions prior to 8.0 is (<literal>'RC4'<\/literal>) which is considered insecure. It is strongly recommended to explicitly specify a secure cipher method. \n\nThe default value for PHP versions prior to 8.0 is (<literal>'RC4'<\/literal>) which is considered insecure. It is strongly recommended to explicitly specify a secure cipher method."],["$iv","string|null","The initialization vector used for decryption of <parameter>data<\/parameter>. It is required if the cipher method requires IV. This can be found out by calling <function>openssl_cipher_iv_length<\/function> with <parameter>cipher_algo<\/parameter>."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openssl_seal<\/function>"]]
["function","Generates a PKCS5 v2 PBKDF2 string\n\n<function>openssl_pbkdf2<\/function> computes PBKDF2 (Password-Based Key Derivation Function 2), a key derivation function defined in PKCS5 v2.",[["$password","string","Password from which the derived key is generated."],["$salt","string","PBKDF2 recommends a crytographic salt of at least 128 bits (16 bytes)."],["$key_length","int","Length of desired output key."],["$iterations","int","The number of iterations desired. NIST recommends at least 1,000. As of 2023, OWASP recommends 600,000 iterations for PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 and 210,000 for PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512."],["$digest_algo","string","Optional hash or digest algorithm from <function>openssl_get_md_methods<\/function>.  Defaults to SHA-1. It is recommended to set it to SHA-256 or SHA-512."]],["string|false","Returns raw binary string or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>hash_pbkdf2<\/function>","<function>openssl_get_md_methods<\/function>"]]
["function","Exports a PKCS#12 Compatible Certificate Store File to variable\n\n<function>openssl_pkcs12_export<\/function> stores <parameter>certificate<\/parameter> into a string named by <parameter>output<\/parameter> in a PKCS#12 file format.",[["$x509","mixed","See Key\/Certificate parameters for a list of valid values."],["$output","string","On success, this will hold the PKCS#12."],["$private_key","OpenSSLAsymmetricKey|OpenSSLCertificate|array|string","Private key component of PKCS#12 file. See Public\/Private Key parameters for a list of valid values."],["$passphrase","string","Encryption password for unlocking the PKCS#12 file."],["$options","array","Optional array, other keys will be ignored. KeyDescription<literal>\"extracerts\"<\/literal>array of extra certificates or a single certificate to be included in the PKCS#12 file.<literal>\"friendly_name\"<\/literal>string to be used for the supplied certificate and key"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
