["function","Checks if a private key corresponds to a certificate\n\nChecks whether the given <parameter>private_key<\/parameter> is the private key that corresponds to <parameter>certificate<\/parameter>.\n\nThe function does not check if <parameter>private_key<\/parameter> is indeed a private key or not. It merely compares the public materials (e.g. exponent and modulus of an RSA key) and\/or key parameters (e.g. EC params of an EC key) of a key pair.\n\nThis means, for example, that a public key could be given for <parameter>private_key<\/parameter> and the function may return <type>true<\/type>.",[["$certificate","OpenSSLCertificate|string","The certificate."],["$private_key","OpenSSLAsymmetricKey|OpenSSLCertificate|array|string","The private key."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if <parameter>private_key<\/parameter> is the private key that corresponds to <parameter>certificate<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
