["function","Strip whitespace (or other characters) from the beginning and end of a string\n\nThis function returns a string with whitespace stripped from the beginning and end of <parameter>string<\/parameter>. Without the second parameter, <function>trim<\/function> will strip these characters:\n\n<literal>\" \"<\/literal>: ASCIISP character <literal>0x20<\/literal>, an ordinary space.\n\n<literal>\"\\t\"<\/literal>: ASCIIHT character <literal>0x09<\/literal>, a tab.\n\n<literal>\"\\n\"<\/literal>: ASCIILF character <literal>0x0A<\/literal>, a new line (line feed).\n\n<literal>\"\\r\"<\/literal>: ASCIICR character <literal>0x0D<\/literal>, a carriage return.\n\n<literal>\"\\0\"<\/literal>: ASCIINUL character <literal>0x00<\/literal>, the NUL-byte.\n\n<literal>\"\\v\"<\/literal>: ASCIIVT character <literal>0x0B<\/literal>, a vertical tab.",[["$string","string","The <type>string<\/type> that will be trimmed."],["$characters","string","Optionally, the stripped characters can also be specified using the <parameter>characters<\/parameter> parameter. Simply list all characters that need to be stripped. With <literal>..<\/literal> it is possible to specify an incrementing range of characters."]],["string","The trimmed string."],["<function>ltrim<\/function>","<function>rtrim<\/function>","<function>str_replace<\/function>"]]
